Z||000000||Jay||07-17-2001||04:20 PM||||Just wondering what everyone is using for oil in their V8's.  Especially the Northstar guys.  I'm moving to synthetic.  Anyone else?<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||07-17-2001||06:37 PM||||Hi Jay,<P>I run Race Proven Mobil 1 Advance Formula 15W-50 fully synthetic in my 350 because there have been terrific reports on it. They even ran an "INDY" engine 500 miles and the cross hatch hone marks were still in the cyclinder bores. Run this weight because my car only gets used during summer cruise season. I also run Castrol Syntec 5W-50 full synthetic when I can't find the Mobil 1 or the Castrol is on a super sale.<P>Both of these will treat your engine real good (try to find a 5 micron oil filter for your engine to). Because your in a slightly cooler climate area, I think the Castrol 5W-50 would be better for you as more wear occurs on cold starts.<BR>Tom||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||07-18-2001||01:40 PM||||hey now, it still hits 100 degrees here in the summer <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!  I don't live in an igloo or anything.  But yeah, I'm also running 5w50 synthetic in my Northstar.  I only drive in summer.||||reg||1
